<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Relación de Michoacán</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1540</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Relación de <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michoacan">Michoacán</a> is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscript</a> of about 1540, compiled by the Franciscan friar Jerónimo de Alcalá from the accounts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purepecha-empire">Purépecha</a> nobles and priests for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">Viceroy</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-de-mendoza">Antonio de Mendoza</a>. Illustrated by native painters, it records the history, religion and government of the Purépecha state and its conquest by the Spanish. It is the main source for Purépecha history and is kept in the library of the Escorial.</p></div>
